// RUN: cd %corpus && ! %zomc compile --check 04-expressions/primitive_str_member_read_capability_neg_66.zom > %t 2>&1
// RUN: %FileCheck %s --input-file %t

// A dot member read on a primitive str value is syntax the parser and binder
// accept, but str is not a nominal scalar with lowered fields. The checker body
// slice drains the free function body with the unsupported-construct code
// ZOM4099 instead of reaching a missing-fact invariant.

// CHECK-LITERAL: Error [ZOM4099]: this function body uses a construct the compiler cannot generate code for yet
// CHECK-LITERAL:   --> conformance/04-expressions/primitive_str_member_read_capability_neg_66.zom:3:12
// CHECK-LITERAL:   |
// CHECK-LITERAL: 3 |     return s.length;
// CHECK-LITERAL:   |            ^~~~~~~~
// CHECK-LITERAL: 1 error generated.
